import ModularFormsKB.Milne.Ch7.Curves
import ModularFormsKB.Milne.Ch6.ModularEquation

/-!
# Milne, Chapter 7: the canonical model of $X_0(N)$ over $\mathbb Q$ (D098)

J. S. Milne, *Modular Functions and Modular Forms*, version 1.31 (`milne2017mf`), Section 7, pdf p. 95.

Milne: let $C$ be the curve $F_N(X, Y) = 0$ over $\mathbb Q$ ($F_N$ the modular polynomial of Theorem 6.1); the
canonical model $X_0(N)_{\mathbb Q}$ is the complete regular curve over $\mathbb Q$ attached to $C$ (Example 7.4), and
$z \mapsto (j(z), j(Nz))$ identifies $X_0(N)_{\mathbb C}$ with $X_0(N)_{\mathbb Q} \otimes \mathbb C$.

By Theorem 7.2 the complete regular curve attached to $C$ is determined by its function field, which is the field of
fractions of $\mathbb Q[X, Y]/(F_N)$, i.e. the field $\mathbb Q(j, j_N)$ generated by $j(z)$ and $j(Nz)$ inside the field
$\mathbb C(X_0(N))$ of modular functions for $\Gamma_0(N)$ ($F_N(j, Y)$ is the minimum polynomial of $j_N$ over
$\mathbb C(j)$, and $F_N$ has rational coefficients). We therefore define: a complete regular curve over $\mathbb Q$ is
**a canonical model of $X_0(N)$** (`IsCanonicalModelX0`) if its function field is isomorphic to the subfield of
$\mathbb C(X_0(N))$ generated by $j$ and $j_N$ (Mathlib's `Subfield.closure`, which contains $\mathbb Q$). The
identification of $X_0(N)_{\mathbb C}$ with the base change of the model to $\mathbb C$ (via Theorems 7.2 and 7.5 and
Theorem 6.1, which says that $j$ and $j_N$ generate $\mathbb C(X_0(N))$ over $\mathbb C$) is not formalized.
-/

open AlgebraicGeometry

noncomputable section

namespace ModularFormsKB.Milne

/-- **The canonical model $X_0(N)_{\mathbb Q}$** (Milne, Section 7, pdf p. 95; D098): a complete regular curve $C$ over
$\mathbb Q$ whose function field $\mathbb Q(C)$ is isomorphic to the field $\mathbb Q(j, j_N) \subset \mathbb C(X_0(N))$
generated by the modular functions $j(z)$ and $j(Nz)$, i.e. to the function field of the plane curve $F_N(X, Y) = 0$
(see the module docstring). -/
@[kb "milne2017mf" "Section 7, canonical model X0(N)_Q (pdf p. 95)"]
def IsCanonicalModelX0 (N : ℕ) (hN : 0 < N) {C : Scheme.{0}} [IsIntegral C] (f : C ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of ℚ)) :
    Prop :=
  IsCompleteRegularCurve ℚ f ∧
    ∃ jX jNX : TauCeti.RiemannSurface.MeromorphicFunction (X0 N), IsJOnX0 N jX ∧ IsJNOnX0 N hN jNX ∧
      Nonempty (C.functionField ≃+* Subfield.closure {jX, jNX})

end ModularFormsKB.Milne
